From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-b2q: give the fold sensor its own input device

The fold hall sensor (SW_LID) sat in the same gpio-keys node as Volume Up,
so both came out as one input device. A client that grabs the volume keys
(EVIOCGRAB, to turn Volume Up + Volume Down into a screenshot chord) then
hid the fold from logind and upower: logind kept the lid state it read
before the grab, reported LidClosed with the phone open, and the main
display went off at every power key press.

Stock keeps them apart (gpio_keys for the volume key, hall_ic for the
fold), so do the same: Volume Up stays alone in gpio-keys, the fold
sensor moves to its own gpio-keys node, labelled "Fold".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
@@ -78,12 +78,19 @@
 			debounce-interval = <15>;
 			linux,can-disable;
 		};
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The fold hall sensor, stock hall_ic "flip" (SW_FOLDER, which is
+	 * SW_LID): low when the phone is closed, 50 ms debounce. Only opening
+	 * wakes the phone. Its own input device, as stock's hall_ic is, so the
+	 * volume key device carries nothing but the volume key: a client that
+	 * grabs the volume keys would otherwise hide the fold from everyone.
+	 */
+	hall-sensor {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+		label = "Fold";
 
-		/*
-		 * The fold hall sensor, stock hall_ic "flip" (SW_FOLDER, which is
-		 * SW_LID): low when the phone is closed, 50 ms debounce. Only
-		 * opening wakes the phone.
-		 */
 		switch-fold {
 			label = "Fold";
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
